n=14 gate/tightness duality probe (codex-2026-05-31 S382)
Convention: k=13 speeds, threshold=1/14.

Residue action on the n=14 unit skeleton
  Unit points are a/14 for a in {1,3,5,9,11,13}.
  A speed with residue r mod 14 covers such a point iff r*a == 0 mod 14.
  residue= 0 covers_unit_points=6
  residue= 1 covers_unit_points=0
  residue= 2 covers_unit_points=0
  residue= 7 covers_unit_points=0
  residue=13 covers_unit_points=0
  Therefore: without a 14-multiple, all six unit points remain safe.

