Interpretation
  No 14-multiple leaves the six unit points a/14 safe.  Such a set can be tight only in the boundary-only sense, with unit witnesses available.
  A genuine open-cover counterexample must destroy those unit witnesses, so it must contain at least one 14-multiple.
  The local evidence supports the complementary heuristic: inserting a 14-gate into the initial tight architecture destroys exact tightness and moves the obstruction to positive gaps or descendant endpoints.
